<h3 id="database-branching" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Database branching</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#database-branching" aria-label="Link to Database branching"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>A branch in Neon is a copy-on-write clone of your database. Branches include both schema and data. Teams use them to create ephemeral environments for development, testing, and preview environments.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Branch creation is instant</strong> - Independent of DB size. Storage is not duplicated for each branch.</li>
<li><strong>Branches are cost-efficient</strong> - You can deploy thousands of branches for $19 /month.</li>
<li><strong>Branch compute can scale to zero when idle</strong> - to further reduce cost.</li>
</ul>
<p>How branches can be used to increase development velocity:</p>
<dl><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="onboard-faster-keep-collaboration-in-sync" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>Onboard Faster, Keep Collaboration in Sync</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#onboard-faster-keep-collaboration-in-sync" aria-label="Link to Onboard Faster, Keep Collaboration in Sync"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"></dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> Give each developer on your team their own branch for local development. They can use <a class="" href="/docs/introduction/point-in-time-restore">branch reset</a> to instantly restore and catch up with the latest changes.</dd><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="one-branch-per-pr" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>One Branch per PR</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#one-branch-per-pr" aria-label="Link to One Branch per PR"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"></dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> Use automation to give each git branch or Pull Request a corresponding database branch. This can be done with automation tools like GitHub Actions, or more easily as part of an integration:</dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> - <a class="" href="/docs/guides/neon-github-integration">Neon GitHub integration</a> - An easier way to create a branch for every PR.</dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"></dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> - <a class="" href="/docs/guides/vercel-overview">Neon Vercel Integration</a> - Create and integrate a branch into every Vercel Preview deployment.</dd><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="ephemeral-environments-for-devtest" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>Ephemeral Environments for Dev/Test</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#ephemeral-environments-for-devtest" aria-label="Link to Ephemeral Environments for Dev/Test"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"></dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> Deploy confidently by using branches to run your test suite on an exact copy of your production database. No handling of seed data, no manual work keeping environments in sync.</dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> - <a class="" href="/docs/use-cases/dev-test">See guide in docs</a></dd><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> - <a class="" href="/blog/from-days-to-minutes-how-neo-tax-accelerated-their-development-lifecycle">Read how others do it</a></dd></dl>
<hr/>
<h3 id="autoscaling" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Autoscaling</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#autoscaling" aria-label="Link to Autoscaling"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>Neon dynamically adjusts the amount of resources allocated to your database in response to the current load, eliminating the need for manual intervention.</p>
<dl><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="performance-w-cost-efficiency" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>Performance w/ cost-efficiency</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#performance-w-cost-efficiency" aria-label="Link to Performance w/ cost-efficiency"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> Your CPU/memory automatically scale up during traffic spikes. When you no longer need the extra resources, your database scales down.</dd><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="no-manual-resizes-for-compute-or-storage" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>No manual resizes for compute or storage</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#no-manual-resizes-for-compute-or-storage" aria-label="Link to No manual resizes for compute or storage"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dd class="pl-6 first:mt-1"> Other platforms require downtime for resizes, limit the frequency of resizes, and don&#x27;t let you scale storage down. On Neon everything is automated and instant.</dd><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="performance-for-high-connections" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>Performance for high connections<br/></span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#performance-for-high-connections" aria-label="Link to Performance for high connections"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt><dt class="relative mt-4 flex items-start font-bold first:mt-0"><span class="mr-2.5">✓</span><span id="neon-has-pbbouncer-built-in-at-no-extra-cost-use-pooling-and-keep-scaling" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight font-bold"><span>: Neon has pbBouncer built-in at no extra cost. Use pooling and keep scaling.</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#neon-has-pbbouncer-built-in-at-no-extra-cost-use-pooling-and-keep-scaling" aria-label="Link to : Neon has pbBouncer built-in at no extra cost. Use pooling and keep scaling."><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></span></dt></dl>
